## Why This Is Asked

This question checks ability to design a runtime-extensible client using plugin registries and per-service routing. It emphasizes dynamic extension without downtime, thread-safety, and clear interfaces.

## Key Concepts

- Plugin registry
- Strategy pattern
- Hot swapping
- Per-service metadata
- Concurrency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Interfaces and registry sketch
interface AuthStrategy { applyHeaders(req, meta): void }
interface RetryPolicy { nextDelay(attempt, err): number; shouldRetry(attempt, err): boolean }
class Registry { registerAuth(key, factory); getAuth(key); registerRetry(key, factory); getRetry(key); }

class ApiClient { constructor(registry) { this.registry = registry } send(req, meta) { const auth = this.registry.getAuth(meta.serviceKey); auth.applyHeaders(req, meta); const retry = this.registry.getRetry(meta.serviceKey); /* use retry */ }
}
```

